                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "In **AI search**, *extractability* is how easily an AI system can **pull a clean, self-contained fact or passage** from your content and reuse it in an answer without losing meaning.[2][5][14]\n\nIt is less about whether the content is *relevant* and more about whether it is **easy to isolate, understand, and quote**.[1][6][11] In practice, highly extractable content is usually **answer-first, clearly structured, unambiguous, and supported by headings, short paragraphs, lists, tables, or schema**.[1][3][15][17]\n\nA simple way to think about it:\n- **Relevance** = is the content about the query?\n- **Extractability** = can the AI cleanly lift a usable answer from it?[1][5][11]\n\nContent with high extractability tends to have:\n- **Self-contained statements** that make sense on their own.[2][4][6]\n- **Clear topic sentences** and explicit relationships between ideas.[3]\n- **Compact sections** that do not depend heavily on surrounding context.[4][15]\n- **Structured markup or formatting** that helps AI systems parse the page.[1][3][17]\n\nIf you want, I can also show you **how to improve extractability on a webpage** or give a **before/after example**.",
